name w2-05-tanks
timeout 6700
time 1981-06-07T12:55:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W2, SORTIE 5 OF 10 - OSIRAK 1981 (OPERATION OPERA): REACH, NOT COMBAT.
# THE SAME RIDE WITH THE TANKS ON. THE ONE MISSION THE SPEC COULD NOT WRITE.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w2-osirak.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: w2-04-loaded.fbm. ONE FACT DIFFERS - the two `set store <n> tank370` lines on the
# PLUMBED stations 4 and 6. Everything else is the same line for line, objectives included.
# THIS SORTIE IS NOT IN THE SPEC AND IT IS THE CAMPAIGN'S OWN SUBJECT: when the spec was written
# `C5` was wholly open and its own headline read "this campaign's first deliverable is not a
# mission file, it is a drop-tank entry in core/FBStore.h and a boom". Half of that landed on
# 2026-07-30 - the tank, not the boom - and this file is what it bought. The dropped spec mission
# whose slot this took is named in the campaign header (sim/campaigns/w2-osirak.fbc).
#
# THE ANCHOR: the package flew "over 1,600 km" for the round trip and was "near the limit of its
# range"; the external tanks were exhausted en route and jettisoned over the Saudi desert [T4]. The
# same source's own straight-line figure is ~1,090 km each way, which does not agree with its own
# round-trip number; MEASURED between the two coordinates the source itself gives (Etzion 29.94/34.87,
# Al-Tuwaitha 33.20/44.52) the great circle is 982.9 km each way, 1,965.9 km out and back [DERIVED].
# ALL THREE FIGURES ARE CARRIED. The campaign compares its measured radius against all of them and
# averages none.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WHAT DOES THE TANK BUY, ON THE SAME JET FLYING THE SAME LEG? THE LADDER
# WAS FLOWN FIRST, as an attribution run outside the ten (campaign file §State); one straight leg at
# 240 m / 400 kt / `fuel_int_pct 100` to fuel exhaustion, one configuration per row:
#   clean                            FLAMEOUT AT 1,492.6 km, 4.6708 lb/km  -> radius   746.3 km
#   2 x Mk-84                        FLAMEOUT AT 1,162.3 km, 5.9984 lb/km  -> radius   581.2 km
#   2 x tank370                      FLAMEOUT AT 2,173.4 km, 5.3022 lb/km  -> radius 1,086.7 km
#   2 x tank370, dropped when dry    FLAMEOUT AT 2,327.9 km, 4.9503 lb/km  -> radius 1,164.0 km
#   2 x Mk-84 + 2 x tank370 (THIS)   FLAMEOUT AT 1,748.8 km, 6.5896 lb/km  -> radius   874.4 km
#   -> THE TANKS BUY 586.5 km ON THE WAR LOAD, +50.5 %, ON +65.3 % MORE FUEL [DERIVED]
#   -> AND THE WAR-LOAD RADIUS OF 874.4 km IS 108.5 km SHORT OF THE ANCHOR'S OWN 982.9 km EACH WAY -
#      11.0 % short, with ZERO reserve, an air start and no taxi/take-off/climb burn in the account.
#      THAT IS THE CAMPAIGN'S CENTRAL NUMBER and it is negative.
# The externals run dry at 675.8 km on this configuration [MEASURED, the tick at which total fuel
# reaches the model's own 6,972.0 lb internal capacity]. The anchor's tanks ran dry "about 1,000 km
# into the flight" [T4] - the same order, from a completely independent direction.
# The leg below is unchanged from both controls: 671.7 km out and back, 90 % of the CLEAN radius.
# WHAT THE NUMBER IS NOT, STATED BEFORE IT IS READ. This jet spawns IN THE AIR at cruise altitude and
# cruise speed. The anchor's aircraft started their engines, taxied, took off and climbed on the same
# fuel, and FlightBox models none of that: EVERY W2 RANGE NUMBER IS AN UPPER BOUND on the flyable
# radius, and the direction of the error is known and one-sided.
#
# THE ARENA: the raid's own outbound track from Etzion AB 29.94000 34.87000 [T4, approximate] on
# bearing 068.37 deg, out to the 671.7 km turn point and back to Etzion. Scale: 1 deg lat = 111,320 m,
# 1 deg lon at 31.570 N = 94,845 m [DERIVED].
#   `w2pit`  target_soft  32.16405 41.41736 - a desert installation at the turn point (campaign rule 3)
#
# WHY THIS FILE STILL DECLARES NO `kill` OBJECTIVE, AND WHY THAT IS THE DISCIPLINED CHOICE. The clean head of this
# ladder, w2-03, carries nothing to attack with, so a `kill` objective here would make the two runs
# differ in TWO things - the stores AND the verdict - and neither difference could then be attributed.
# The objectives are identical in all three files of this ladder; the kill is read out of
# `UNIT_RESULT` beside the fuel.
# THE SIX STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURES, in short form (full text in w2-01-dome.fbm):
#   1. `C5` HALF CLOSED, AND THIS FILE IS THE HALF THAT LANDED. Two `tank370` feed the ENGINE's own
#      fuel books (JSBSim `FGTank` contents, draw priority external-before-internal written as one
#      integer per tank), not a second account beside them. AERIAL REFUELLING IS NOT BUILT AND IS NOT
#      APPROXIMATED: this jet launched full and never takes another pound, so the anchor's tanker-free
#      profile is reproduced exactly and nothing here says what a tanker would have been worth.
#   2. `C20` open, `--elev const`, 0 m plane; the real ground under this route is 42.83-1,599.22 m
#      (MEASURED, listed in w2-02-ingress.fbm). Etzion itself is at 523.59 m, so this jet flies its
#      whole ride 283.59 m BELOW its own airfield.
#   3. `C10` - level laydown. Nothing is released: the four stores are here for their mass, their
#      drag and, for two of them, their fuel.
#   4/5/6 - no F-15, `FirstFlightKo`, W1's fixed point: all irrelevant, this is a single jet alone.
#
# READING RULE (binding): the exit code is NOT the measurement. Read, in this order: (1) `fuelLbs` in
# the LAST telemetry row - the campaign contract §2 requires every mission to report it and this is the
# file it was written for, (2) whether both `nav WP_REACHED` lines appear, (3) the ground distance
# flown. A run that lands with reserve to spare has not tested the thing this raid was about; a run
# that does not get home has answered the campaign's central question in the negative.

# MEASURED (fingerprint a92dfa00db6f4837, exit 0): 179.0 km SHORT BECOMES 2,373.4 lb IN HAND.
#   the leg       both waypoints reached, `idx=1` at t=6,575.2 s - 1.7 s EARLIER than the clean
#                 control despite 4,552 lb more fuel and four more stores, because the tanks are dry
#                 and out of the fuel account long before the turn
#   fuel          11,523.8 lb at t=0 (`sms TANK_LOADED` twice, 2,276 lb each) -> 2,373.4 lb in the
#                 last row, where its control had 0.0 and was 179.0 km from home
#   the ladder    the tanks are worth +586.5 km / +50.5 % on the war load and +680.8 km / +45.6 %
#                 clean, on +65.3 % more fuel (A1). Dropping them when dry is worth another 154.5 km
#   THE CAMPAIGN'S CENTRAL NUMBER, and it is negative: the war-load radius is 874.4 km against the
#   982.9 km the anchor needed each way - 11.0 % SHORT, with zero reserve, zero combat allowance, an
#   air start that burns nothing on the ground and a straight line where the raid flew a dog-leg. The
#   externals run dry at 675.8 km [MEASURED] against the anchor's "about 1,000 km into the flight"
#   [T4] - the same order from an entirely independent direction.

unit w2rad5
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 29.94000 34.87000 240 68.4 400        # Etzion AB, on the raid's own outbound bearing
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100                        # 6,972 lb internal - the SAME internal load as w2-03
  set store 3 mk84                            # the war load, unchanged from the control ...
  set store 7 mk84
  set store 4 tank370                         # THE ONE FACT: 2,276 lb in the left wing tank ...
  set store 6 tank370                         # ... and 2,276 lb in the right one. 11,523.8 lb aboard
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  wp 32.16405 41.41736 240 400                # THE TURN POINT: 671.7 km out = 90 % of the measured radius
  wp 29.94000 34.87000 240 400                # home, the same 671.7 km back
  objective waypoints
  objective survive

unit w2pit5
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 32.16405 41.41736 ground 68.4 0
